  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "In a large pan heat the olive oil over a medium-high heat. Add the red onion and the garlic and cook for 2 minutes, being careful not to burn the garlic. Add the eggplant to the pan and cook for 5 minutes on each side until golden and soft - you may need to add extra olive oil because of how thirsty eggplant tends to be!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/552f35a66ced6e3e4f8b4571/step_556eb179af698.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the cumin to the pan and stir for 1 minute or until fragrant. Now add the tomatoes, chickpeas, red wine vinegar, and the white wine, cover the pot with a lid and cook for 10 minutes or until the tomatoes have softened and everything has fused together. Season with salt and pepper along the way.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/552f35a66ced6e3e4f8b4571/step_556eb179c085c.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the couscous in a bowl and pour the boiling water over the couscous, stir with a fork, and then cover the bowl tightly with cling wrap, leave to sit for 5 minutes. Remove wrap and then begin to fluff the couscous with a fork. Season well with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/552f35a66ced6e3e4f8b4571/step_556eb179d3834.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide the couscous and eggplant braise between bowls, top with a dollop of yoghurt and then garnish with a good sprinkle of fresh coriander and some lemon juice for a nice fresh taste. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/552f35a66ced6e3e4f8b4571/step_556eb179e989a.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
